+# UI design review: HUD and daily reward popup
+
+**Reviewed:** `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/Hud.luau`, `UI/DailyReward.luau`, and
+`Main.client.luau` (the wiring), read from the code. No screenshots or build were checked. The
+review covers what the code shows across phone (landscape, designed first), tablet, PC, and Xbox,
+in every state the code can reach.
+
+**Player and moment:** mostly children aged about 6-12 on landscape phones, with a smaller PC and
+Xbox audience. The HUD shows during building. The daily reward popup opens **the moment the player
+joins**.
+
+**Not checked (needs the Device Emulator):** real pixel positions against the top bar on each
+device, how the layout looks at `PreferredTextSize = Largest`, and Xbox behaviour in the
+Controller Emulator. Each finding says when it needs one of these checks.
+
+## Severity scale
+
+| Severity | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| **Blocker** | Stops play for a platform or a whole group of players, or puts the experience at moderation risk. Fix before the next release. |
+| **High** | Most players hit it, or it misleads or pressures children. Fix in the polish pass. |
+| **Medium** | Hurts readability, consistency, or comfort for many players. Fix in the polish pass if you can. |
+| **Low** | Cleanup or future-proofing. |
+
+Evidence labels: `[study]` controlled research, `[standard]` Roblox docs or platform/standards
+bodies (WCAG, Xbox Accessibility Guidelines (XAG)), `[practitioner]` community or design-system
+practice, `[inference]` reasoned from those, `[unverified]` not confirmed. The labels show how
+strong each claim is. Where a fix is only `[inference]`, treat it as a default to playtest.
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
