+
+---
+
+## Findings, ranked by harm to play
+
+### 1. Discord link in the HUD breaks the Community Standards (Blocker)
+
+**What goes wrong:** `Community` shows "Join our Discord for free codes! discord.gg/blockbuilders"
+on screen at all times. Roblox UI "may not link to, share, or display URLs of any external
+websites or services", and other attempts to send users off Roblox are also banned. Social Links on
+the experience page are the only allowed route `[standard]`. This puts the whole experience at
+moderation risk, and it sends children to an off-platform chat service. (Principle 9.)
+
+**Fix:** Delete the `Community` label. If you want to promote the community, add a Social Link on
+the experience or group page (the owner must be age-checked 16+). Don't gate it on
+`PolicyService.AllowedExternalLinkReferences`, because that always returns an empty list
+`[standard]`. To give out free codes, put an in-game code box in Settings and announce codes
+through Roblox channels. Player-typed codes are checked on the server, so they don't need text
+filtering. Filter anything you show back to the player.
+
+### 2. Xbox players can't press any button, so the join popup traps them (Blocker)
+
+**What goes wrong:** Every button (menu buttons, Claim, Close) listens on `MouseButton1Click`,
+which only fires for the mouse. `GuiButton.Activated` fires on mouse release, touch release, and
+gamepad A `[standard]`. Nothing sets a gamepad selection either. An Xbox player joins, the
+reward popup covers the screen, and they can neither claim nor close it. Their only escape is
+gameplay input under a dimmed screen. The menu is unreachable on gamepad, and there are no
+keyboard shortcuts on PC. (Principle 5.)
+
+**Fix:**
+- Switch every `MouseButton1Click` to `Activated`.
+- Popup: when it opens, call `GuiService:Select(panel)` with **Claim** as the default selection.
+  Wrap the panel in a `SelectionGroup` with `SelectionBehavior = Stop` so focus stays inside the
+  modal. B closes the popup. Check B-to-close in the Controller Emulator, because whether a
+  `ContextActionService` B binding runs before Roblox's own B handling isn't documented
+  `[unverified]`. When the popup closes, return focus to whatever opened it.
+- HUD menu: bind a gamepad button (for example D-pad Right) to focus the menu rail, using a
+  `SelectionGroup` with `Escape`. Bind PC keys (for example `I` Inventory, `R` Rewards, `Esc`
+  closes the panel). Show glyphs from `UserInputService:GetImageForKeyCode`, and never hardcode
+  Xbox art `[standard]`.
+- Give every button a visible `SelectionImageObject` so focus is easy to see on a TV.
+
+### 3. A full-screen popup blocks play on join (Blocker)
+
+**What goes wrong:** `rewardOpen = source(true)` dims the whole screen with an `Active` frame
+before the player has placed a single block. Players try 24 or more experiences a month and decide
+"within minutes" `[standard]`. Children treat clutter that looks like an ad as an obstacle and
+leave when they get stuck `[study]`. Your first impression is a sales-style popup, not your game.
+(Principle 1.)
+
+**Fix:** Don't open the popup on join. Show a red badge (a dot or "1") on the Rewards button while
+a reward waits, and let the player open it when they choose. If you want more reach, auto-open it
+once per session **after** a natural break (for example after the player's first build is placed,
+or after about 2 minutes) and never mid-action `[inference]`. Measure the change with a join →
+first block placed funnel (see Playtest and funnel questions).
+
+### 4. The menu sits in the bottom-right thumb corner, on top of the jump button (Blocker on touch)
+
+**What goes wrong:** `Menu` is anchored at `(1, -12, 1, -12)`, the bottom-right corner. On phones
+the jump button and the right thumb live there `[standard]`. Players will jump when they meant to
+open the inventory, or open Settings mid-jump, and the buttons hide the jump control. Small targets
+at screen edges are especially hard for children `[study]`. (Principle 3, zone map.)
+
+**Fix:** Move the rail to the **right edge at middle height**, vertically centred
+(`AnchorPoint (1, 0.5)`, `Position (1, -16, 0.5, 0)`) on phones. Tablets need it lower, about
+60-65% down and still clear of the jump button, because 40% down is hard to reach there
+`[standard]`. On PC and Xbox, a bottom-middle or right-edge rail both work. Pick one and keep it in
+the same place everywhere (Principle 7). Choose the layout from `PreferredInput` (see #18). The
+`CoreUISafeInsets` fix in #5 doesn't avoid the thumbstick and jump button, so keep this placement
+explicit `[inference]`.
+
+### 5. The coin counter is drawn under Roblox's top bar (High)
+
+**What goes wrong:** `IgnoreGuiInset = true` switches the ScreenGui to `DeviceSafeInsets`, which
+avoids notches but **not** Roblox's core UI `[standard]`. Coins sit at `(8, 8)` in the top-left,
+where the Roblox menu and chat buttons have been since November 2023. The coin count, the one
+number players watch, is partly hidden, and tapping it may open the Roblox menu. Verify in the
+Device Emulator.
+
+**Fix:** Remove `IgnoreGuiInset`, or set `ScreenInsets = Enum.ScreenInsets.CoreUISafeInsets`
+explicitly, for the HUD ScreenGui. Put the popup's dim backdrop in its own ScreenGui with
+`ScreenInsets = None` so it still covers the full screen, and leave the panel in a
+`CoreUISafeInsets` gui. Move coins to the top-middle or top-right, clear of Roblox's buttons. If
+you want them inside the top-bar strip, read `GuiService.TopbarInset` live; the top bar grew from
+36 to 58 px and "may vary" `[standard]`. Don't use `TopbarSafeInsets`: since December 2025 it has
+zero height on consoles `[practitioner]`.
+
+### 6. The HUD may disappear for good after the first respawn (High, verify)
+
+**What goes wrong:** `HudGui` is created in code inside `PlayerGui` with the default
+`ResetOnSpawn = true`, and `Main.client.luau` runs once from StarterPlayerScripts. Guis with
+`ResetOnSpawn` are cleared on respawn, and nothing in this script rebuilds the gui
+`[standard; inference]`. If a player resets or falls off the map, coins and the menu vanish until
+they rejoin.
+
+**Fix:** Set `ResetOnSpawn = false` on `HudGui` (and on the popup's gui if you split it out).
+Verify: start a test, reset the character, and confirm the HUD is still there.
+
+### 7. Streak-loss threat with a 59-second countdown aimed at children (High)
+
+**What goes wrong:** The popup says "Claim in 0:59 or lose your 6-day streak! Come back every day
+so you don't lose your progress." It combines a loss threat, a live countdown, and a guilt nudge to
+return. That is the pattern ICO Standard 13 and the FTC's dark-patterns work flag for children's
+services, and those are this game's working bar `[standard; inference]`. The 59-second window also
+punishes a child who glances away. The timer keeps running after the popup closes and stops at
+`0:00`, with nothing explaining what happened. (Principle 9.)
+
+The sentence is also about 110 characters of wrapped text for a reader who skips paragraphs
+`[study]`. With `TextScaled`, it shrinks to fit 64 px of height and comes out small.
+
+**Fix:**
+- Replace it with one positive line: **"Day 7 reward: 50 coins!"**. After claiming, say **"Next
+  reward tomorrow"**, with no countdown.
+- Make the streak forgiving: a missed day pauses the streak instead of resetting it, or allow one
+  grace day. Keep the countdown out of the UI entirely `[inference]`.
+- `REWARD_WINDOW_SECONDS = 59` looks like a test value. The real window belongs to the server's
+  day boundary, not a client loop.
+
+### 8. Players can claim the reward again and again; the tiles break after day 7 (High)
+
+**What goes wrong:** `claimReward` has no "already claimed today" state. After claiming, the
+Rewards button reopens the popup with Claim still live, so every press adds 50 coins and a streak
+day. After day 7 no tile is green, so the popup shows no "today" at all. Players will find and
+share the exploit, and the popup stops making sense. (Principle 7: a progression button never
+changes what it does.)
+
+**Fix:** Add a claimed-today state, shown both on the button and in the popup:
+- Claim becomes disabled and reads **"Claimed ✓"**, plus "Next reward tomorrow".
+- The Rewards badge from #3 disappears.
+- After day 7, the streak loops to a new week, or day 7 repeats as the top reward. Decide which
+  and show it.
+
+The claim itself has to go to the server. Right now coins and the streak are set on the client.
+That's outside this UI review, but the UI should show a busy state on Claim while the server
+replies, if the reply takes longer than 1 s `[standard]`.
+
+### 9. Menu buttons are blank orange squares; names show only on mouse hover (High)
+
+**What goes wrong:** All icons are `rbxassetid://0`, so the menu shows three identical orange
+squares. The only names are in a tooltip that opens on `MouseEnter`. Touch and gamepad have no
+hover, and they are about 83% of the audience `[standard]`, so those players can't tell Inventory
+from Settings. Children can't be asked to work out what icons mean; labels beside icons
+"take the guesswork out" `[standard]`. (Principles 2, 5.)
+
+**Fix:** Give each button an icon and a short label under it ("Bag", "Rewards", "Settings"), with
+the label inside the hit area. Delete the hover tooltip, or keep it on PC only as a preview of the
+same text. Don't ship until real icon ids exist. Use one icon style and color for all three
+`[standard]`, and a distinct color only for the reward badge.
+
+### 10. Touch targets are far too small (High)
+
+**What goes wrong:** Menu buttons are 36 px on touch (32 on PC), Close is **24 x 24**, and Claim,
+the primary action, is 120 x 36. Children aged 7-11 miss touch targets 46% of the time, against
+32% for adults `[study]`. The working rule is 10 mm or more per target and 15-20 mm for primary
+actions `[study; practitioner]`, which is about 44 UI units or more, with primary actions larger
+`[practitioner]`. (Principle 3.)
+
+**Fix:**
+
+| Element | Now | Target |
+|---|---|---|
+| Menu buttons (touch) | 36 x 36, 6 px gap | 60 x 60 graphic plus label, 10 px or more gap |
+| Close (X) | 24 x 24 | 48 x 48 hit area (the glyph can stay smaller), at least 8 px in from the panel corner |
+| Claim | 120 x 36 | 220 x 64 or larger |
+
+Make hit areas larger than the visible graphic: put a transparent button around a smaller image.
+Single taps only, with no holds.
+
+### 11. The fixed 520x340 panel doesn't fit small landscape phones (High)
+
+**What goes wrong:** On a small phone in landscape, the usable height after insets is often under
+340 units, so the top (title, Close) or the bottom (Claim) gets cut off. Verify on the Device
+Emulator's smallest phone. All sizes are pixel offsets with no scaling, so the same panel looks tiny
+on a 4K TV. (Principle 4.)
+
+**Fix:** Size the panel from the screen, for example
+`Size = UDim2.fromScale(0.9, 0.85)` with a `UISizeConstraint` (max 560 x 380, min 300 x 260), and
+lay out its contents with `UIListLayout` and padding so they reflow. Or adopt the root `UIScale`
+pattern from the `vide` skill's `references/screens.md` and test the smallest phone, a tablet,
+1080p, and the Xbox emulator. Either way, Claim must stay on screen at `PreferredTextSize` Largest.
+
+### 12. Popup text and tiles fail contrast; tile states differ only by color (High)
+
+**What goes wrong:** Approximate WCAG ratios, worked out by hand from the color constants. The
+minimum is 4.5:1 for text and 3:1 for large text and inactive items `[standard]`.
+
+| Pair | Ratio | Passes? |
+|---|---|---|
+| Title orange (255,170,0) on panel (240) | about 1.7:1 | No, even as large text |
+| Body and Close gray (150) on panel (240) | about 2.6:1 | No |
+| White on Today and Claim green (80,200,90) | about 2.2:1 | No |
+| White on Future tile (200) | about 1.7:1 | No |
+| White on Claimed tile (130) | about 3.9:1 | Large text only |
+
+Claimed (130 gray) and Future (200 gray) are also told apart **only** by shade (about 2.3:1 between
+them), and Today only by hue. Color-blind players and anyone in sunlight on a phone can't tell which
+days they've earned. Color must never carry meaning alone `[standard]`. (Principle 6.)
+
+**Fix:**
+- Title: dark text (for example 40,40,48) with an orange accent bar or icon, or an orange title on a
+  dark header strip.
+- Body and Close: dark gray, 60 or darker on 240, which gives at least 7:1.
+- Green surfaces: darken the green (about 30,130,50) or use dark text on the current green.
+  Check every pair with a contrast checker before shipping.
+- Tile states, each with a second cue:
+  - **Claimed:** a check mark plus a dimmed tile.
+  - **Today:** a thick outline, a slightly larger tile, and a "Today" label.
+  - **Future:** the reward icon at normal strength, with no check.
+- Multiply the backdrop's `BackgroundTransparency` by `GuiService.PreferredTransparency` and update
+  it when that changes `[standard]`.
+
+### 13. The Rewards button pulses forever, with no reduced-motion option (Medium)
+
+**What goes wrong:** The Rewards button scales ±8% at about 1 Hz from a `Heartbeat` connection,
+always, even after the reward is claimed. Motion pulls the eye, so a pulsing button competes with
+building `[study]`, and Roblox asks for animated cues "in moderation" `[standard]`. It ignores
+`ReducedMotionEnabled` `[standard]`. Writing to the scale every frame also redraws the whole HUD
+ScreenGui every frame `[standard, via roblox-performance]`.
+
+**Fix:** Show a static badge while a reward is unclaimed (see #3). If you want motion, play one
+short pop (about 300 ms) when the reward becomes available, then stop. With
+`ReducedMotionEnabled`, skip the pop and show only the badge. Drop the per-frame connection
+entirely.
+
+### 14. The toast lasts 1.5 s; the reward moment is thin (Medium)
+
+**What goes wrong:** "+50 coins" shows for 1.5 s as bare orange text in the center, while the
+popup snaps shut. Children read slowly, and auto-dismissing messages need about 6 s at least
+`[practitioner]`. Claiming a reward is the "moment of joy" this flow exists for `[standard]`, but
+it gets one weak channel and no sound. (Principle 8.)
+
+**Fix:**
+- On Claim, celebrate inside the popup before it closes:
+  - Today's tile pops (scale to about 1.15 and back in 200-300 ms) and gets its check mark.
+  - A coin sound plays.
+  - A few coin icons fly to the coin counter, which ticks up.
+
+  That's two or three channels, a medium amount of juice, which beats both none and extreme
+  `[study]`. Then the popup closes itself after about 1 s, or on a "Nice!" button.
+- If you keep a toast, put it in the upper middle on a backplate, show one at a time, and keep it
+  up for `max(6 s, words / 3.5 + 1 s)` `[inference]`. Merge repeats ("+50" then "+100").
+- With reduced motion on, skip the flying coins and pops; the check mark and the counter update
+  still happen.
+
+### 15. HUD text has no backplate or outline over the 3D world (Medium)
+
+**What goes wrong:** "Coins: 250" is white with no backing, and the toast is orange with no
+backing. Over a bright sky, white blocks, or sand, they become unreadable. Contrast is measured
+against the least contrasting part of the scene `[standard]`.
+
+**Fix:** Put the coin counter on a rounded, semi-opaque dark pill (background about 0.3
+transparency, scaled by `PreferredTransparency`), with a coin icon and the number, and drop the
+word "Coins:". Give the toast the same pill, or white text with a 2 px black `UIStroke`.
+
+### 16. Day tiles don't show what the player gets (Medium)
+
+**What goes wrong:** The tiles show only the numbers 1-7. A child can't see what tomorrow's reward
+is, which takes away the positive reason to come back that should replace the threat in #7.
+
+**Fix:** Each tile shows the reward icon and amount ("50") under a small "Day 3" caption. Make
+day 7 visibly bigger or special. With 7 tiles of 64 units or more, the row needs the panel width
+from #11. On narrow phones, two rows (4 + 3) also work.
+
+### 17. `TextScaled` everywhere ignores the player's text-size setting (Medium)
+
+**What goes wrong:** Every label uses `TextScaled`. That opts out of
+`GuiService.PreferredTextSize`, the player's own text-size setting `[standard]`, and makes labels of
+the same role come out at different sizes `[practitioner]`. Long strings (the streak line, a big
+coin count) shrink until they're tiny.
+
+**Fix:** Use one `TextSize` per role: title about 32, body about 20, button about 24, HUD counter
+about 24, all authored at 1080p. Let containers grow with `AutomaticSize`. Verify at Largest text
+size: nothing clips, and Claim stays on screen. Leave 30-40% spare width on fixed labels for
+translation `[practitioner]`. Body text should reach 18 px at 1080p on PC and 26 px on Xbox
+`[standard]`.
+
+### 18. `TouchEnabled` picks the layout; no TV or 4K scaling (Medium)
+
+**What goes wrong:** `IS_MOBILE = UserInputService.TouchEnabled` is true on touch laptops and
+handhelds `[standard]`, and it's read once, so a player who switches between touch and a gamepad
+keeps the wrong layout. Nothing scales the UI for 10-foot viewing on Xbox.
+
+**Fix:** Pick the layout from `UserInputService.PreferredInput` (Touch, Gamepad, KeyboardAndMouse)
+and re-evaluate when it changes. Use `GuiService.ViewportDisplaySize` (`Large` means a TV) to
+increase sizes and keep UI inside a TV-safe margin. Roblox gives no figure, so about 5% is the
+usual habit `[inference]`. Don't use `IsTenFootInterface` (deprecated).
+
+### 19. No press feedback, open/close motion, or sound (Low)
+
+**What goes wrong:** Buttons rely on the default `AutoButtonColor` at most. The popup pops in and
+out instantly. Nothing makes a sound, even though console menus are expected to play selection
+sounds `[standard]`.
+
+**Fix:**
+- Every press changes visibly within 100 ms (scale to about 0.95, or darken) and plays a short
+  click.
+- The popup enters in 200-300 ms with ease-out (fade the backdrop, scale the panel from 0.9) and
+  leaves in about 200 ms with ease-in `[practitioner]`.
+- With reduced motion on, use a plain fade or no tween at all.
+- Gamepad focus moves play a soft tick.
+
+### 20. Gotham font (removed in 2024) and a coin count with no number format (Low)
+
+**What goes wrong:** Gotham was removed in May 2024 and is now drawn as Montserrat `[standard]`, so
+what you see isn't what you specified. Coin counts grow without limit, and with `TextScaled` the
+label just shrinks.
+
+**Fix:** Use Builder Sans (the platform font) for body text and Builder Extended or a bold weight
+for titles. Format coins with one suffix table for the whole game (1,250 → "1.25K", about three
+significant digits) so the label width stays stable `[inference]`.
+
+---
+
+## What works (keep it)
+
+- The menu is short: three buttons, one route to each place. Keep it this short when you add
+  icons and labels.
+- The popup uses a centered modal with a dim backdrop, and Today is highlighted. That's the right
+  structure; only the timing, sizing, contrast, and copy need work. The reactive sources in
+  Main (`coins`, `streakDays`, `rewardOpen`) make the fixes above straightforward to wire.
+
+## Playtest and funnel questions
+
+These are questions the design can't settle. Run a playtest with about five fresh players, mostly
+children on phones, plus one on Xbox `[standard]`.
+
+1. **Join funnel:** log `join → first block placed → reward opened → reward claimed`. Compare
+   auto-open on join (current) against a badge only. Use an Experiment only if the game has about
+   1,000 daily users or more `[standard]`; otherwise compare before and after.
+2. Can children name each menu button from its icon and label alone, without help?
+3. On the smallest phone, do players hit jump by accident when using the new right-edge rail?
+   Count missed taps on Close and Claim.
+4. Can an Xbox tester claim, close the popup, and open each menu with no mouse and no instructions?
+5. Does day-7 retention change after the streak-loss wording and countdown are removed? Track D1
+   and D7 return rates before and after.
+6. At `PreferredTextSize = Largest`, does every label fit without clipping (Device Emulator
+   screenshot check)?
